    "created_at": "2024-08-27T21:55:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-27T21:55:19Z",
    "body": "That's a great point about the high bits \u2014 it would violate `bits.Add`'s guarantee that carryOut is 0 or 1 if the high bits were not cleared.\r\n\r\nIn any case, `MOVL $0, AX; SETCS AX` or `XOR AX, AX; SETCS AX`  still would be an improvement over `SBBQ / NEGQ`. It's the same number of instructions, but the zeroing idiom would break the data dependency on AX and cut the dependency chain to three instructions.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
